      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14231667/assets/ed4fb3bd21624b15349fd520c2944389d81af99d81962fa54b815628fd7360aa.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠B={35}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({35}^{∘}) & =\\frac{x+2}{2x} \\\\ 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({35}^{∘}) & =x+2 \\\\ 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({35}^{∘})-x & =2 \\\\ x(2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({35}^{∘})-1) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({35}^{∘})-1} \\\\ x & =4.994\\,8…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x=2(4.994\\,8…)=9.989\\,6…, \\\\ AC & =x+2=(4.994\\,8…)+2=6.994\\,8….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(9.989\\,6…)(6.994\\,8…) \\\\  & =34.937\\,8… \\\\  & ≈34.9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.",
